    cleets:terminalTargetShare 0.8835 .

cleets:EVAdoptionPrediction a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "EV adoption prediction"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Model output for one LAD, quarter and scenario. Not an observed value."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cleets:Observation .

<https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#activity/diffusion-q2026rev> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Bounded logistic diffusion capped by the fleet turnover path" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Companion notebook to \"Predicting electric vehicle adoption in Wales from open data integrated in semantic knowledge graphs\" (manuscript, 2026): EVAdoptionWalesPredictionsModels24Nov.ipynb, export diffusion_scenarios_to_2045.csv."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Per-district logistic curves (rate, midpoint) are fitted independently to the quarterly adoption share, private battery-electric cars (VEH0142) over private cars (VEH0105), 2011 Q4 to 2025 Q4, recency-weighted. The reported trajectory is the lower, in every predicted quarter, of the district's fitted curve and its own fleet turnover path. The path is a stock-flow model started from the private cars licensed at 2026 Q2 by fuel and year of first registration (VEH9901): cars leave at the scrappage rates observed for British cohorts (VEH1111), cars enter private keepership at the ages at which they do so in each district, new and second hand, and the battery-electric share of new cars rises from 24.7% in 2026 to 80% in 2030 and 100% in 2035 (new pure petrol and diesel car sales end in 2030; every new car is zero emission from 2035). Central scenario: this rule with the scrappage rates of 2021 to 2025. Low: the 2030 level cut to 50%. High: the scrappage rates of 2014 to 2019. Counts are the share multiplied by the district's private cars at 2026 Q2; the petrol and diesel cars remaining, hybrids included, are those cars less the predicted battery-electric cars." ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-24T20:06:15+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH0105>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH0142>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH1111>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH9901> ;
    cleets:notebookStage "Sections 6 and 7 of the companion notebook (export in Section 13)" ;
    cleets:paperSection "Sections 4.2 and 4.6 (methods); 5.4, 5.6, 5.7 and 5.8 (results)" .

